{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused","id":1412083,"title":"Evasion Penalties? Really confused...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-05T07:45:36-07:00","id":1412083,"title":"Evasion Penalties? Really confused...","content":"Finally got myself into a DB game (fingers crosseddd) and want to play an Air Stylist. Air Dragons Sight says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reading her foe\u2019s movements through the slight disturbances they create in the air, the Immaculate could dodge his attacks blindfolded. She ignores (Perception/2, rounded up) total points of onslaught penalties or <b>environmental penalties</b> to her Evasion. </div> </div> </div>Threshold Warding Stance also mentions environmental penalties to Evasion. So I go back to the core to check what environmental penalties I can ignore. I cant find any. The section on penalties has stuff for combat penalties like fighting in the dark or on slippery rocks, but it says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bonuses and penalties also occasionally affect a character\u2019s static values. In these situations, the static value is simply raised or lowered by the amount specified. </div> </div> </div>This means penalties don't <b>always </b>reduce Evasion, only if they specifically say they do. Wound penalties specifically do it. Armor Mobility penalties specifically do it. Being prone specifically does it, and does it separately from attack penalties. But being blind doesnt, and missing an arm doesn't, and poison says nothing about static values, and same for difficult terrain.<br /> <br /> So okay, Air Dragons Sight basically just affects onslaught penalties and maybe weird Charm stuff elsewhere that inflicts environment penalties to Evasion. Got it. But then I find this, which is <b>also </b>in the core book:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fivefold Bulwark Stance ignores wound penalties, onslaught penalties, penalties from being grappled, and penalties incurred from being hit by temporary physically crippling techniques other than those that affect the senses. However, it is <b>vulnerable to attacks that cripple the senses</b>, such as those that cause <b>blindness </b>or dizziness, and attacks which physically stun the Solar (such as Ox-Stunning Blow). <b>Poisons and illusions</b> may also cut through the Solar\u2019s Defense through use of this Charm. Thus Fivefold Bulwark Stance deals handily with the most common group attack tactics, but is vulnerable to more specialized tactics. </div> </div> </div>So how does this work? Do poison and blindness affect Evasion? Do the environmental combat penalties in the core affect Evasion? The book says they dont, but then there are multiple Charms for Solars/DBs to ignore the penalties the core says don't exist. Help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1538-jonsonjonson","name":"JonsonJonson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T08:16:11-07:00","id":1412090,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell an environmental penalty to evasion would be fighting in the dark or fighting in tight quarters.<br /> <br /> The rule of thumb is that any penalty that isn't explicitly part of basic rules or part of a Charm effect, falls in the realm of ST fiat. I can't think of any Charm that specifies it inflicts environmental penalties to Evasion, but if you used a power that made a room dark (or just plain old killed the lights) the ST could give anyone who can't see in the dark a penalty to Evasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T08:56:13-07:00","id":1412103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412090#post1412090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I can tell an environmental penalty to evasion would be fighting in the dark or fighting in tight quarters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought so too... except the core gives those as examples of &quot;martial penalties&quot; on page 188, the same page it says that you dont apply penalties to static values unless it specifically says to. So thats directly against what the book itself says.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412090#post1412090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule of thumb is that any penalty that isn't explicitly part of basic rules or part of a Charm effect, falls in the realm of ST fiat. I can't think of any Charm that specifies it inflicts environmental penalties to Evasion, but if you used a power that made a room dark (or just plain old killed the lights) the ST could give anyone who can't see in the dark a penalty to Evasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I get they can do that, because theyre the ST. They can do whatever. But where does it <b>say </b>to do that? Is there a sidebar or errata or dev comments anything? Or is this just a house rule, which feels like a weird thing to buy a Charm for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1538-jonsonjonson","name":"JonsonJonson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T09:05:22-07:00","id":1412104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JonsonJonson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused#post1412083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This means penalties don't <b>always </b>reduce Evasion, only if they specifically say they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how you draw that conclusion from the lines that you've cited.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T09:28:34-07:00","id":1412105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412104#post1412104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how you draw that conclusion from the lines that you've cited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay the full section is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bonuses or penalties add to or subtract from the character\u2019s relevant dice pool by the number indicated. For example, a character suffering under a divine curse that levels a -2 penalty to all attempts to transgress the laws of the city Great Forks would lose two dice from her dice pool every time she attempted an action that broke the city\u2019s laws.<br /> <br /> Bonuses and penalties <b>also occasionally</b> affect a character\u2019s static values. In these situations, the static value is simply raised or lowered <b>by the amount specified</b>. </div> </div> </div>So there are penalties (which they give a bunch of examples of) and they reduce your dice pool. But <b>sometimes </b>those penalties affect static values (like Evasion). And if they do, you reduce it <b>by the amount they say</b>. So it only happens if they specifically tell you a penalty reduces your Evasion.<br /> <br /> They do that on wound penalties, onslaught penalties, mobility penalties, and prone penalties... but not for darkness or tight spaces or poison or disease or whatever. So those don't reduce your Evasion. Prone lists a dice penalty and an Evasion penalty separately. So does Flurrying.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also there are a bunch of poisons with a -3 penalty, so that would be a -3 Defense to anyone who gets bitten by a snake, which seems crazy? Same for Joint-Wounding Attack which is a Solar Charm that gives a stacking -3 penalty on all dice pools for a decisive attack - theres no way that hits Defense, that would be nuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1538,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1538-jonsonjonson","user":"JonsonJonson","date":". 09-05-2020, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1538-jonsonjonson","name":"JonsonJonson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T10:46:14-07:00","id":1412113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JonsonJonson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412105#post1412105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Also there are a bunch of poisons with a -3 penalty, so that would be a -3 Defense to anyone who gets bitten by a snake, which seems crazy? Same for Joint-Wounding Attack which is a Solar Charm that gives a stacking -3 penalty on all dice pools for a decisive attack - theres no way that hits Defense, that would be nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joint wounding attack specifies dicepools only so it\u2019s probably only affecting your rolled pools and not your static values, but poisons that give -3 absolutely affect your Parry and Evasion by giving a flat -3 to them. That\u2019s why charms like Dipping Swallow are amazing.<br /> <br /> An environmental penalty that affects your evasion is anything that is in the environment, so not your wounds or poison or onslaught, that might make dodging harder. If you\u2019re fighting in ankle deep sucking mud that\u2019s a -1 or -2. If you\u2019re fighting in pitch black that\u2019s -3, if you\u2019re fighting in pitch black on a slick wet surface that might be -5. <br /> <br /> Now, fighting in pitch blackness also gives an attacker -3 to his attack pools if he can\u2019t see you as well, but static values get punished more than rolled pools.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now on the other hand since you ARE an air dragon with Air Dragon Sight and Threshold Warding Stance if you can arrange to fight an enemy in the pitch black on unstable footing you\u2019ll rip them apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T11:26:00-07:00","id":1412122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412113#post1412113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joint wounding attack specifies dicepools only so it\u2019s probably only affecting your rolled pools and not your static values, but poisons that give -3 absolutely affect your Parry and Evasion by giving a flat -3 to them. That\u2019s why charms like Dipping Swallow are amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but <b>where does it say that</b>, though? Because the Poison section just says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Penalty, a penalty that is applied to all actions the character takes while poisoned </div> </div> </div>So as far as I can tell, they dont apply to Parry or Evasion at all?<br /> <br /> Like compare that to Wound Penalties:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As your character accumulates damage in his health track, he receives a dice penalty to all rolled actions indicated by the highest number associated with a health level which has received damage. <b>This wound penalty also applies to all of your character\u2019s static values, such as Defense and Resolve</b>. </div> </div> </div>Or Mobility Penalties:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mobility Penalty: This is the number of dice heavier armor subtracts from all nimbleness-based Athletics rolls, as well as from any rolls involving chases, running, and dodging. Most armor is noisy and this same number is subtracted from Stealth rolls involving attempts to move silently. <b>Finally, this value is subtracted directly from the wearer\u2019s Evasion score</b>. </div> </div> </div>Or Prone Penalties:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certain attacks (such as Smashing attacks made by hammers, or being thrown by a grappler) can leave a character prone\u2014knocked forcefully to the ground. A prone character must take a rise from prone combat action (see p. 198) to regain his footing. As long as a character is prone, he <b>suffers a -1 penalty to his Parry, a -2 penalty to his Evasion</b>, a -3 penalty to attacks, and cannot take any movement actions other than to rise from prone. </div> </div> </div>Why would poison penalties apply to Defense? The book never says they do?<br /> <br /> And it doesnt say anything about darkness or blindness (-3 penalty to &quot;actions which primarily depend on sight&quot;) affecting my Defense, either. Or difficult terrain, which gives me a -3 penalty to a few specific actions but never mentions Defense. Where is this all coming from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1538-jonsonjonson","name":"JonsonJonson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T12:28:38-07:00","id":1412136,"title":"","content":"Ex3 isn\u2019t like DnD 3.5 where there\u2019s morale bonuses, insight bonuses, competence bonuses, etc, etc, and any and all bonuses fall into those catagories. <br /> <br /> For example Sight without Eyes in Solar Archery specifies that it\u2019s ignores sight based penalties to archery attacks, but you\u2019ll notice there\u2019s no specific sight based penalties in the penalties section. The Storyteller can just freely apply any penalties to any action as appropriate. Firing an arrow in the eyeball of a catagory 5 hurricane is a -5 Penalty as appropriate.<br /> <br /> When the book says \u201cit reduces your static values by the specified amount\u201d it means that -3 penalty isn\u2019t applied to your dicepool that\u2019s used to make your Evasion, it just flat out reduces your evasion by the amount specified, which is 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:07:51-07:00","id":1412147,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re paying a little too much attention to that one paragraph and not to the one after it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Equipment and Charm modifiers are generally pre-set, depending on the magic or equipment being employed. Situational penalties, on the other hand, are set by the Storyteller whenever it seems appropriate to do so (see below). </div> </div> </div>While static value penalties do seem to be made out to be the exception rather than the rule, it\u2019s perfectly valid for the Storyteller to \u201cspecify\u201d one.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1205717#post1205717\">Also someone did Ask the Devs this two and a half years ago.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T13:40:21-07:00","id":1412156,"title":"","content":"Okay, I don't normally say this, but darkness not affecting your defence is fucking stupid. Sonebidy swinging a sword or firing an arrow at you, and the only indication you have of where it is is the sound of it cutting through the air, and that's not going to hamper your ability to duck out of the way, or interpose your weapon properly at all. Sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T15:47:41-07:00","id":1412175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JonsonJonson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412103#post1412103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought so too... except the core gives those as examples of &quot;martial penalties&quot; on page 188</div> </div> </div> </div>The examples of Martial Penalties are Situational Penalties that apply in combat. &quot;Martial Penalty&quot; is a kind of &quot;Situational Penalty&quot;, much like &quot;Vision Based Penalty&quot; is a Situational Penalty. Exalted 3E uses &quot;natural language&quot; not well-defined system terminology.<br /> <br /> Generally, Martial Penalties don't apply to Static Values, but occassionally they do. This is at ST discretion, more on this below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JonsonJonson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412122#post1412122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would poison penalties apply to Defense? The book never says they do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1163439#post1163439\">the devs have clarified that poison penalties do apply to Defense</a>.<br /> <br /> I understand your frustration, 3E Core was very badly editted. A lot of the rules are unclear or in obtuse places.<br /> <br /> Generally, you're correct: things do what they say they do. Blindness doesn't say it affects your Defense, so it doesn't (normally) affect your Defense.<br /> <br /> And that makes sense from a gameplay point of view: if you have the attacker taking a penalty to their attacks, and the defender taking a penalty to their defense, why bother, right? Blindness is a Flaw: it only really affects you as an optional way to gain XP. The general rule is logical.<br /> <br /> Likewise, a Charm like Joint-Wounding Attack which specifies that it reduces dice pools shouldn't generally penalize defense. The Charm does what it says it does -- no more, no less.<br /> <br /> But Exalted also has, *sigh* the Orichalcum and Storyteller's Rules. If your attacker can see in the dark and you can't, the ST is supposed to adjudicate that by making stuff up on the fly: like, you take -3 to actions and -1 to defense. Likewise, if the ST asks you to make a Difficulty 2 roll to escape your pursuers, then whilst technically Joint-Wounding Attack can't help you, the ST has every right to say that you can escape automatically by burying a throwing knife in your pursuer's leg. This isn't spelled out neatly for you, but allow me to try and crib quote the Corebook for you here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Orichalcum Rule:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> This is a big game with lots of </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">rules, set in an even bigger and more complex world, and </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">players are endlessly inventive. If you ever find that by </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">following the letter of the rules, you get a result that </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">doesn\u2019t </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">make sense</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> in the course of the story, </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">the rules are wrong, </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">the story is right</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">. If the rules suggest something dumb or </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">nonsensical or just plain not fun, ignore them or change </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">them. Story comes before adherence to the rules.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Storyteller\u2019s Rule:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> A lot of the rules in </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Exalted</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">, es</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">-</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">pecially the combat engine, are heavy abstractions rather </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">than faithful simulations. Storyteller, if it seems to you </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">like a player is using the letter of the rules to muck up the </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">spirit of the game and the fun of the story, then that par</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">-</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">ticular rules loophole doesn\u2019t work. You are explicitly </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">empowered to call shenanigans whenever it seems nec</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">-</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">essary\u2014the rules can\u2019t account for everything, and any </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">interpretation of a Charm or other mechanic away from </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">its intended function isn\u2019t legal unless you say it is.&quot; p282</span><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:serif\">Defense:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> A </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">static value</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> which establishes how difficult it </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">is for others to attack the character, based on the higher </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">of the character\u2019s </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Evasion</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> or </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Parry</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">.&quot; p183<br /> <br /> &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">static value:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> A fixed value generated by a character\u2019s </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">traits, used as a difficulty rating for hostile individuals</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">attempting to act on the character in certain ways. </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Exalted</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">has static values: </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Defense</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Evasion</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Guile</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Parry</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">, and </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Resolve</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">.&quot; p183<br /> <br /> &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">When a character takes an action in </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Exalted</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">, her chance </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">of success is represented by her </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">dice pool [...] </span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rather than generating dice pools, characters occasion</span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">ally generate static values\u2014fixed ratings which are re</span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">-</span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">corded on the character sheet. These are normally used </span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">to determine the difficulty for hostile individuals to act </span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">on the character\u2014for example, a character\u2019s Defense </span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">rating [...] </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Having determined what dice pool to use, the Storyteller </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">then considers the task the player wants his character to </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">attempt and assigns it a </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">difficulty rating</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">.</span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot; p185</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Your dice pools may be changed by </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">modifiers</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2014bonuses or </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">penalties that increase or decrease a character\u2019s likelihood </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">of success by adding or subtracting dice from her dice pool. </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The most common sources of modifiers in </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Exalted</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> are </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">sit</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">-</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">uational penalties</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> (penalties based on the circumstances in </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">which the action is attempted), </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">equipment modifiers</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">(bonuses or penalties based on tools used to assist or hamper </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">the action), and </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Charm modifiers</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> (bonuses or penalties </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">based on the use of magic to assist or impede the action).</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Bonuses or penalties add to or subtract from the character\u2019s </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">relevant dice pool by the number indicated. For example, a </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">character suffering under a divine curse that levels a -2 </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">penalty to all attempts to transgress the laws of the city Great </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Forks would lose two dice from her dice pool every time </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">she attempted an action that broke the city\u2019s laws.</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Bonuses and penalties also occasionally affect a charac</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">ter\u2019s static values. In these situations, the static value is simply raised or lowered by the amount specified. [...] </span><u><b><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Situational penalties [...] are set by the Sto</span></b></u><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><u><b>ryteller whenever it seems appropriate to do so</b></u> (see below)</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">&quot; p188 (Emphasis added)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">&quot;[W]</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">hat if the Night Caste hero Har</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">monious Jade attempts to shoot a marauding Abyssal in </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">the middle of a cloudy night, with a high wind blowing? </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">In this case, the difficulty of the action remains unchanged, </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">but the archer suffers a penalty to her dice pool. </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Penalties may also be applied when there is no diffi</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">culty, as in the case of opposed rolls. [...] </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">A list of example penalties follows, demonstrating how </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">characters might be hampered by certain factors:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">&quot; p188</span><br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Poisons and illusions may also cut through the Solar\u2019s </span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Defense&quot; p349</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Long story short: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25285_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25285\" data-vbnamecard=\"25285\">Epitome</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13313_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13313\" data-vbnamecard=\"13313\">Sith_Happens</a> are right (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page688\">here's a repost of the dev ruling Sith_Happens posted above</a>). Perhaps this will be addressed in the upcoming ST guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-05-2020, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T16:33:31-07:00","id":1412183,"title":"","content":"Sidetrack:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412156#post1412156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I don't normally say this, but darkness not affecting your defence is fucking stupid. Sonebidy swinging a sword or firing an arrow at you, and the only indication you have of where it is is the sound of it cutting through the air, and that's not going to hamper your ability to duck out of the way, or interpose your weapon properly at all. Sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>My rationalization here is three-fold.<br /> <br /> Firstly, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/VebE-ZMQ9CQ?t=135\" target=\"_blank\">it's a genre conceit</a>. A <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yke3ur99P2g\" target=\"_blank\">common</a> genre conceit. A <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZuqwMQTc8cE\" target=\"_blank\">really common</a> genre conceit. A <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8VUIq6dwMyM\" target=\"_blank\">too common</a> genre conceit, that's really funny when played for laughs. Plus <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B66feInucFY\" target=\"_blank\">The Exalted have superpowers</a>.<br /> Secondly, Blindness is either a way to gain XP or it's a penality from a Charm: it doesn't have to be overly punishing as a gameplay mechanic.<br /> Thirdly, darkness is kinda a great equalizer. Sure it's harder to dodge in the dark. It's also harder to hit in the dark. Instead of giving attacks -9 and defenses -3, they just gave attacks -3. Dipping Swallow Defense was already good enough, and they didn't want Solars fighting all their enemies in perfect darkness. But you can always adjudicate the penalty on the fly at the table. Or give really good Stunt Bonuses based on how characters interact with the darkness.<br /> <br /> But if that doesn't fly with you, just houserule that the -3 applies to Defense as well. Simples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-05-2020, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T00:36:45-07:00","id":1412231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JonsonJonson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412105#post1412105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also there are a bunch of poisons with a -3 penalty, so that would be a -3 Defense to anyone who gets bitten by a snake, which seems crazy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it crazy because you assert that being bitten by a snake is a super common occurrence that would severely undermine the integrity of Defence, or because you don't buy that being bitten by a venomous snake is a big deal?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T20:33:51-07:00","id":1412378,"title":"","content":"Well it <i>is</i> only a difficulty 1 gambit to throw a snake at someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T01:21:26-07:00","id":1412403,"title":"","content":"Previous editions did specify &quot;coral snake venom&quot;. The coral snake being one of the most deadly in North America, its venom being a powerful, paralyzing neurotoxin that completely shuts down the heart and lungs. -3 defence seems pretty appropriate. Hemlock, a -4, was used in the ancient world in place of anaesthetic (plus, you know, killing folks like Socrates).<br /> <br /> No assassin is poisoning their blade with Jararaca venom. And if your PC gets bitten by a Golden Tree Snake, then they're not going to take worse than a -1 (if that). But, yeah, deadly snake bite at -3 seems fine to me.<br /> <br /> And if deadly snake venom doesn't seem deadly enough to anyone, remember these are rules for PCs. The heroes with the kind of True Grit required for Exaltation, and the foes who stalk them. The ST is supposed to say Johnny Trivial Opponent simply dies if he's bitten by a snake or cut with a poison blade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-07-2020, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T07:09:58-07:00","id":1412715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412183#post1412183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My rationalization here is three-fold.<br /> <br /> Firstly, <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/VebE-ZMQ9CQ?t=135&quot;]it's</a> a genre conceit[/URL]. A <a href=\"http://&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yke3ur99P2g&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">common</a> genre conceit. A <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZuqwMQTc8cE&quot;]really</a> common[/URL] genre conceit. A <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8VUIq6dwMyM&quot;]too</a> common[/URL] genre conceit, that's really funny when played for laughs. Plus <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B66feInucFY&quot;]The</a> Exalted have superpowers[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>True, bt that\u2019s what charms are for. Dancing around a-la Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon atop the bamboo forest is a genre conceit but that doesn\u2019t mean everyone gets Graceful Crane Stance for free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1412083-evasion-penalties-really-confused?p=1412183#post1412183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thirdly, darkness is kinda a great equalizer.</div> </div> </div> </div>It usually is, but I\u2019m more concerned about when it isn\u2019t. Like for example Mortwights. They have a supernatural darkness effect that blinds and living creature, but not the dead. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible that this would encourage PCs to try to constantly fight in the dark, but that\u2019s not always so easy. If the room is full of lit torches/candles with a big roaring fire in the fire place you might spend more actions putting out the light than just fighting normally. Otherwise, I say good clever use of your skills to fight blind, like Arya Stark blowing out the candle to fight her rival in the dark. It goes for other things too, fighting a Water Aspect in waist high water is just a bad idea, but clever use of magic to half flood the basement you\u2019re in before fighting down there.<br /> <br /> Then again if there was something like a Super winterbreath jar that made the ground ice out three range bands and my players were just constantly icing every single place they ever battled in to get the penalty on the enemy and ignore it themselves that could get pretty old pretty fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}